Theorem IA-5-step-1: Intraprocedural alias-transfer soundness (6-case enumeration)

  Preconditions:
    - Per Annex E §AIMS IA-5 step (1) clause: "backward transfer of
      forward" — destination's accumulated demand transfers to source via
      seq_add for Cardinality + Consumption + max for Locality
    - Six instruction-shape cases per §6 IA-5 statement:
        (a) Let { Var(v) } — transparent alias
        (b) Project { value } — borrow (composes with TF-14)
        (c) Select { cond, t_val, f_val} — conditional alias to both branches
        (d) Construct / Reuse / CollectionReuse — aggregate builders
        (e) Set { base, field, value } — in-place mutation
        (f) Apply / ApplyIndirect / Invoke / InvokeIndirect / PartialApply /
            RcInc / RcDec / IsShared / Reset — non-aliasing definitions
    - Case (a) Let { Var(v) } transparent alias:
        src.cardinality := seq_add(src.cardinality, dst.cardinality)
        src.consumption := seq_add(src.consumption, dst.consumption)
        src.locality := max(src.locality, dst.locality)
    - Case (b) Project — composes with TF-14 (TF-14.proof):
        src.cardinality := seq_add(src.cardinality, dst.cardinality)
        src.locality := max(src.locality, dst.locality)
        src.consumption := seq_add(src.consumption, Affine)
        no TF-11 demand
      An L-9-excluded scalar destination instead contributes RawDemand selected
      only by liveness: deadProjection when dead, (Once, Affine) when live.
      The live contribution is capped at one copy-out regardless of downstream
      scalar copy count.
    - Case (c) Select { cond, t_val, f_val } conditional alias:
        t_val.cardinality := seq_add(t_val.cardinality, dst.cardinality)
        t_val.consumption := seq_add(t_val.consumption, dst.consumption)
        t_val.locality := max(t_val.locality, dst.locality)
        f_val.{cardinality, consumption, locality} := same (parallel update)
        cond receives only TF-11 (cond, Once)
    - Case (d) Construct / Reuse / CollectionReuse aggregate builders:
        for each arg:
          arg.locality := max(arg.locality, dst.locality)
          arg.access := Owned (unconditional promotion)
        Cardinality NOT transferred (Construct uses each arg once)
    - Case (e) Set { base, field, value } in-place mutation:
        value.access := Owned (unconditional promotion)
        value.locality := max(value.locality, base_state.locality)
        SetTag has no value operand — step (1) is no-op
    - Case (f) non-aliasing definitions — step (1) no-op; only step (2)
      TF-11 demand applies. Step (2) is proven at TF-11.proof.
    - L-6 monotonicity (per Annex E §AIMS IA-5 + §1.2 / §1.3 / §1.5):
      seq_add monotone over Consumption + Cardinality; max monotone over
      Locality; unconditional Owned promotion preserves order
      (Borrowed <= Owned per ACCESS_CARRIER)
    - Cardinality and Consumption updates compose as RawDemand evidence during
      the complete block walk; canonicalization is an observation after the
      fold, never an instruction-local side effect.

  Soundness property:
    Forall arc_instr in ArcInstr. Forall (src, dst) state pair where dst
    state has been accumulated at the backward walk.
      ia5_step1_transfer(arc_instr, src, dst) produces source-side mutation
      per the case-specific rule above
    AND src.{cardinality, locality, consumption} are monotone in dst.{...}
        for fixed src (L-6 layer (b) — seq_add + max monotone)
    AND Access promotion to Owned preserves order (Owned is TOP of
        ACCESS_CARRIER lattice)
    AND Let/Select full-alias transfer and Project/TF-14 transfer project
        exactly into RawDemand.seqAdd
    AND scalar Project transfer composes the TF-14 live/dead copy-out theorem
    AND every permutation of a block's raw instruction contributions produces
        the same unobserved block-entry demand.

  Proof obligation:
    Case coverage plus monotonicity and raw-fold timing:
      (a) Let { Var(v) } transparent alias enumeration — verify
          seq_add(Cardinality) + seq_add(Consumption) + max(Locality).
      (b) Project borrow — verify composes with TF-14 (TF-14.proof) +
          confirm no TF-11 demand emitted.
      (c) Select conditional alias — verify both branches receive full
          demand transfer via seq_add; cond receives only TF-11.
      (d) Construct / Reuse / CollectionReuse aggregate builders — verify
          locality transfer + unconditional Owned promotion for each arg;
          verify Cardinality NOT transferred.
      (e) Set in-place — verify value.access := Owned + value.locality :=
          max(value.locality, base_state.locality); verify SetTag is no-op.
      (f) Non-aliasing definitions — verify step (1) no-op for the 8
          non-aliasing variants; step (2) TF-11 demand applies via TF-11.proof.
      (g) Monotonicity sweep — enumerate L-6 layer (b) over Locality x
          Cardinality x Consumption for cases (a) / (c); confirm Owned
          promotion preserves order for cases (d) / (e).
      (h) Raw block-walk composition — prove Let/Select and Project transfer
          projections use the shared RawDemand algebra; compose the scalar
          Project live/dead copy-out cap; and prove permutation invariance for
          the block's left fold before observation.

    Part (a) — Let { Var(v) } transparent alias:
      Pick representative (src, dst) pairs over the per-dimension carriers
      and verify each component:
        out.cardinality == seq_add_K(src.cardinality, dst.cardinality)
        out.consumption == seq_add_C(src.consumption, dst.consumption)
        out.locality == max_L(src.locality, dst.locality)
        out.access == src.access (no promotion at case a)
        out.uniqueness == src.uniqueness (not propagated)
        out.shape == src.shape (not propagated)
        out.effect == src.effect (not propagated)

    Part (b) — Project borrow:
      Composes with TF-14 (TF-14.proof Part (a)). The IA-5 step (1) Project
      case is structurally identical to TF-14's
      propagate_project_source_demand mutation set:
        src.locality := max(src.locality, dst.locality)
        src.cardinality := seq_add(src.cardinality, dst.cardinality)
        src.consumption := seq_add(src.consumption, Affine)
      AND no TF-11 demand emitted (TF-11.proof Part (a) row "Project").

    Part (c) — Select conditional alias:
      For Select { cond, t_val, f_val } with destination dst, BOTH t_val
      and f_val receive the full demand transfer:
        t_val.{c, k, l} := (seq_add(t_val.c, dst.c), seq_add(t_val.k, dst.k),
                            max(t_val.l, dst.l))
        f_val.{c, k, l} := (seq_add(f_val.c, dst.c), seq_add(f_val.k, dst.k),
                            max(f_val.l, dst.l))
        cond gets only TF-11 (cond, Once)
      Rationale (lives at Annex E §AIMS IA-5 + §3 TF-11 table Select
      row): conditional branches each receive the FULL demand because the
      backward analysis must conservatively assume either branch may
      execute — demand is path-summed across branches, not lattice-max'd.
      Negative witness: if the demand were `max` rather than `seq_add`,
      Select { cond, x, x } (both arms = same variable x) would underweight
      x's demand (only one usage counted instead of two — see TF-11.proof
      Part (b) QTT-consistency).

    Part (d) — Construct / Reuse / CollectionReuse aggregate builders:
      For each arg:
        arg.locality := max(arg.locality, dst.locality)
        arg.access := Owned (unconditional)
        arg.cardinality, arg.consumption — UNCHANGED at step (1); step (2)
          TF-11 adds (arg, Once) demand on Construct/Reuse/CollectionReuse
          per TF-11.proof Part (a).
      Rationale (per Annex E §AIMS IA-5): local struct field cleanup
      at scope exit needs Owned for RcDec emission. Cardinality is NOT
      transferred because Construct consumes each arg exactly once (the
      single-use is already captured by TF-11 step (2)).

    Part (e) — Set in-place:
      Set { base, field, value }:
        value.access := Owned
        value.locality := max(value.locality, base_state.locality)
        base direct via TF-11 (base, Once)
      SetTag { base, tag }:
        step (1) is no-op — no value operand
        base direct via TF-11 (base, Once)
      Verified: ia5_step1_set_promotion() returns Owned for value.access
      and max(value.locality, base_state.locality) for value.locality
      across all input combinations.

    Part (f) — non-aliasing definitions:
      For arc_instr in {Apply, ApplyIndirect, Invoke, InvokeIndirect,
      PartialApply, RcInc, RcDec, IsShared, Reset}:
        ia5_step1_transfer(arc_instr, src, dst) = no-op (returns src
          UNCHANGED)
      Step (2) TF-11 demand still applies (proven at TF-11.proof Part (a)
      for the non-PartialApply rows; PartialApply uses TF-12 + TF-13 per
      TF-12.proof + TF-13.proof).
      Verified: ia5_step1_non_aliasing_noop() returns src for each of the
      8 non-aliasing arc_instr.

    Part (g) — L-6 monotonicity sweep:
      Enumerate the L-6 layer (b) check:
        forall dst1 <= dst2 (per dimension). forall src.
          ia5_step1_transfer(arc_instr, src, dst1) <=
          ia5_step1_transfer(arc_instr, src, dst2)
      Cases (a) + (b) + (c): seq_add monotone over Consumption +
        Cardinality + max monotone over Locality per L-6 layer (a)
        (proven at §02).
      Case (d): max monotone over Locality; Owned promotion is
        unconditional — preserves order (Borrowed <= Owned).
      Case (e): same as (d).
      Case (f): no-op is trivially monotone (identity function).

    Part (h) — RawDemand block-walk composition:
      IA5_full_alias_uses_raw_demand_composition proves that transparent Let
      and conditional Select transfer project to componentwise RawDemand.seqAdd.
      TF14_uses_raw_demand_composition proves that Project contributes
      `(dst.cardinality, Affine)` through the same algebra without observing it.
      TF14_scalar_project_copy_out_sound proves that an L-9-excluded scalar
      destination contributes deadProjection when dead or exactly
      `(Once, Affine)` when live, independent of downstream scalar copy count.
      IA5_block_walk_raw_fold_permutation proves that any permutation of the
      block contribution list has the same foldl result from RawDemand.zero.
      The observation timing and concrete CN-1 negative witness are discharged
      by TF11_raw_demand_timing_sound in the same compiled Lean module.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) sweep over 6-case ArcInstr
        dispatch per section_04::verify_ia5_step1_alias_transfer)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — 6-case instruction-shape enumeration per
        section_04::verify_ia5_step1_alias_transfer)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; max + seq_add monotone per
        L-6 layer (a))
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; IA-5 step (1) does NOT
        call refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge IA-5 step (1) via 6-case ArcInstr enumeration + L-6 monotonicity sweep + composition with TF-14 + TF-11 step (2)
